WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.340
Well, I liked all the Smash games
when they came out,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.920
I liked Smash 64 and I liked Melee a lot.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.840
I just played the game a lot for a few years

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.920
and then I found out that there's
tournaments, so I was like,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.720
"hmm, let me try to be the best at that."

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.000
And then two years later I was the best.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.160
Over the course of his 12-year career

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.560
Jason "Mew2King" Zimmerman
has been known as many things.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.200
He's been the best Super Smash Bros. Melee
player in the world.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:40.540
[Caster audio]

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.720
One of the five gods of Smash,

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.340
a frame data pioneer,

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.100
the only player to be ranked number one
in both Melee and its sequel

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.820
Super Smash Bros. Brawl at the same time.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.690
Right when I start tournaments 
people put me Top 25 in the world pretty fast,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:00.000
Top 25... I was a ranked 15th pretty quickly.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.980
And then I became rank 1 about a year and half later.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.900
But above all else 
Mew2King is proof that if you work hard enough,

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.000
you can be the best.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.940
Mew2King was born on February 5th, 1989,
in Cinnaminson, New Jersey.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.380
and became obsessed with
video games at a young age.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.600
On his old websites
he listed endless records he had in games

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.012
like F-Zero GX,

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.900
Mario Kart Double Dash,

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.660
and, of course, Super Smash Bros. Melee.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.580
But when M2K started playing competitively,

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.200
he failed to make a mark.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.100
Simply put, he just wasn't that good.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.160
He wasn't a natural by any means,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.520
but he had a work ethic, 
at the time, that was unmatched

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.620
and for most players still is unmatched.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.560
You can only get so good off never playing a human

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.860
that knows anything about the game.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.320
Of course their first time is gonna be like,

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.520
"oh, well, you have a lot to learn."

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.220
that's natural.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.720
There isn't much footage of that
time in Mew2King's life,

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.800
because no one cared about a player
who couldn't succeed.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.460
He decided to do his homework and study.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.760
Mew2King spent hours upon hours amassing information about the game.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.540
If he wasn't good at the game,
he needed to know everything about it:

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.500
frame data,

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.560
percentages,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.540
recovery time,

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.120
get-up attack,

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:14.680
ledge grab,

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.240
item stats,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:15.800
grab ranges,

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.340
invincibility timers,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:16.860
priority,

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.360
movement speed,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:17.860
escape formula,

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.360
fall speed,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.920
everything.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.340
M2K pioneered data on Melee.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.780
He knew things no one else would for years

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.680
and he shared it online.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.560
I was a kid alone and I was just like,

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.960
kind of a kid who's just curious about everything

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.540
and I was like, "hmm, I wonder how fast this move is,"

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.660
or I wonder how far this goes, just curious.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.480
And just being curious
makes you just want to know things

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.180
By year 2005 he started entering
real tournaments and started climbing

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.320
fast.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.420
He went from twenty third, to ninth, to third.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.900
At MLG New York M2K placed seventh.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.540
At MLG Dallas he fell to eighth, but he kept pushing.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.800
Third in Chicago,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.660
fourth in Las
Vegas,

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.380
second in Long Island,

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.180
first at Evo East

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.180
and first at Evo West.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.780
He wasn't just good,

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.020
he was constantly getting better.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.380
By 2007 he went from being an unknown scrub

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.680
to a contender for the best in the world.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.780
He was caught in a 3-way race
with Daniel "KoreanDJ" Jung

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.340
and Christopher "PC Chris" Szygiel for
the title of best in the world.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.920
But their struggle was put aside momentarily

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.700
with the release of Super Smash Bros. Brawl.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.920
Brawl was a slower less complicated game

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.640
and one that most melee players didn't like,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.640
but M2K saw Brawl as different,
not necessarily worse,

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.680
and started grinding once again.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.960
Obviously and then Brawl came out in '08 and I was like,

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.980
"let's try to be the best at that,"

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.820
then I became the best at that.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.200
Mew2King was the top ranked
Melee and Brawl player in the world

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.280
from 2008 to 2009.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.360
The melee scene was stagnating,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.320
but M2K was still one of the best and he
proved it at Revival of Melee.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.860
MLG had pulled out of smash in 2007,

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.720
so the community returned to their grassroots nature

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.380
and put on the biggest melee tournament
since the release of Brawl.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.400
I told Alucard from New York,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.800
"okay if you host a ROM (Revival of Melee)

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.800
and you invite Mango, then I'll go."

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.940
Then I'll go and I'll have more motivation to actually care.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.900
Cause right now is just
beat everyone for free except Mango.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.940
And that's actually funny
because that's actually what happened,

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.720
because I beat everyone for free except Mango.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:05:33.880
[Caster audio]

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.040
M2K worked his way through the bracket until he faced

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.740
Bronson "DaShizWiz" Layton in the losers' finals.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:06:04.580
[Caster audio]

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.320
Despite his incredible play Mew2King
started building up bad press.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.860
The once revered player became a controversial figure

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:16.300
after several bracket manipulation incidents
came to light.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:21.000
As a result, M2K was banned from the 2010 MLG finals

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.900
after he took $500 from Wyatt "ADHD" Beekman,

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.060
who beat him in the losers' finals.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:32.640
In May 2011 Mew2King, ADHD and
Jason "ANTi" Bates

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.380
were given yellow cards for splitting their prize money

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:38.040
following Mew2King's fourth place forfeit.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.620
Later that year at Genesis 2,
Mew2King was given a red card

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:45.440
for allegedly sandbagging in pools.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.100
M2K defended himself by saying,
he wasn't in a good mood during the sets

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.400
and claiming pot splitting
was common practice back then.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.900
But the damage was done,
Mew2King's image was shot and Smashers

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.900
were spreading rumors and exaggerating
tales of Mew2King being awkward,

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.200
or otherwise embarrassing.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.520
After late 2010, it was like a three-year time period

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.440
where I was kind of soul-searching in life.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.780
I just didn't really have motivation for whatever.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.820
While M2K became a
growing meme within the community

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:19.100
and the only way to silence the haters
was to conquer them.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.000
Mango: "Uhh"

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.980
M2K: "Follow me on Twitch... and MVG"

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.340
Mango: "What was that, what are you a baby?"

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.440
M2K: "Shut up!"

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.760
Mango: "Alright guys, I'll see you later, umm"

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.320
M2K: "I'm leaving!"

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.400
In late 2013, Mew2King won
17 straight melee tournaments

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.600
after not having taken a major in nearly a year.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:43.160
His slump didn't matter, the controversies vanished,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.160
but since then Mew2King has struggled.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.480
The release of Super Smash Bros 4 Wii U
effectively killed Brawl.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.480
And while M2K was extremely strong in
Smash 4 at the start

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:55.880
he could not keep it up.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.960
He leaned back on Melee, where he has continued to

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.240
consistently place in the top eight,

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.360
but he isn't dominating anymore.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:12.500
[Caster audio]

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.700
He might not finish in first place every time,

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.800
but he's always a contender.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:31.140
[Caster audio]

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.240
Simply put you can never
count out Mew2King.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.080
He's taken first place at at least one Melee tournament

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.560
every single year since 2006.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:43.940
And he didn't do it through raw skill
or having the best practice partners.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.020
He did it by doing his homework

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.320
studying more and working harder

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.520
than almost any Smasher in the business.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.160
He is proof that anyone can win,

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.720
anyone can be the best,

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.800
anyone can stay the best,

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.220
that the king can always return.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.560
Mew2King is more than a god.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.720
Mew2King is an institution.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.100
Thanks for watching!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:13.340
If you want more great content
be sure to hit that subscribe button!

